---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EarnCalc from "../components/EarnCalc.astro";
import HeroScenes from "../components/HeroScenes.astro";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
import Plans from "../components/Plans.astro";
import Roadmap from "../components/Roadmap.astro";
---
<Base title="amader.cloud: second jobs for old devices" description="We wipe, rebuild and look after old phones, TV boxes, laptops and routers, and put them to work as private clouds, cameras, Wi\u2011Fi, screens and school labs for Dhaka homes, buildings, shops and schools." ogDescription="Old phones, TV boxes, laptops and routers, rebuilt into managed infrastructure for Dhaka homes, buildings, shops and schools." hasHero>
<!-- Hero: a slideshow of real Dhaka scenes, each with the second jobs that place really has -->
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
<HeroScenes />
  <div class="node-tip" role="status" hidden></div>
  <div class="wrap hero-content">
    <h1 id="hero-title">Dhaka's next data centre is sitting in its drawers.</h1>
    <p class="bn-line" lang="bn">পুরনো যন্ত্র, নতুন কাজ</p>
    <p class="lede">Old phones, TV boxes, laptops and routers still work. We get the value back out of them, for families and for companies: a new job, or income from the capacity they aren't using. Then we look after them.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-bulb" href="#earn">What could my devices earn?</a>
      <a class="btn btn-line" href="companies.html">For companies</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-investors mono"><a href="investors.html">Investing in reuse? Read the investor overview</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Value: the one idea, for people and for companies -->
<section class="section value" id="value" aria-labelledby="value-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">What we do</span>
      <h2 id="value-title">Idle devices still have value. We get it back out.</h2>
      <p>A device either does a new job, or earns from the capacity it isn't using. We collect, wipe, rebuild and look after it, for people and for companies.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="value-grid" role="table" aria-label="Two ways to get value back, for people and for companies">
      <div class="vg-corner" role="columnheader"></div>
      <div class="vg-col" role="columnheader"><span class="mono">01</span> Give it a job</div>
      <div class="vg-col" role="columnheader"><span class="mono">02</span> Rent out what it isn't using</div>

      <div class="vg-row" role="rowheader"><svg class="pict inline" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-home"/></svg>For people</div>
      <div class="vg-cell" role="cell" data-col="Give it a job"><svg class="pict " aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-photo-cloud"/></svg><p>A private photo cloud, a camera for the stairs, Wi‑Fi on the roof, a screen for notices, and backups your neighbours keep safe.</p><a href="devices.html">What can my device do?</a></div>
      <div class="vg-cell" role="cell" data-col="Rent out what it isn't using"><svg class="pict " aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-coins"/></svg><p>Spare disk space and idle computing earn credit off your plan, and later bKash. A building can pool its earnings towards the service charge.</p><a href="#earn">Estimate your earnings</a></div>

      <div class="vg-row" role="rowheader"><svg class="pict inline" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-briefcase"/></svg>For companies</div>
      <div class="vg-cell" role="cell" data-col="Give it a job"><svg class="pict " aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-server"/></svg><p>Old desktops as file servers and meeting-room screens, tablets as visitor logs, phones as cameras. Or a certified wipe, and the laptops go to school labs.</p><a href="companies.html">For companies</a></div>
      <div class="vg-cell" role="cell" data-col="Rent out what it isn't using"><svg class="pict " aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-moon-desktop"/></svg><p>Office desktops rent out their computing overnight, and spare disks hold encrypted backups, all inside a sandbox that can't see company files.</p><a href="companies.html#earn">How companies earn</a></div>
    </div>
    <p class="small" style="margin-top:18px">For public bodies, we also size digital projects to the real need before they're bought. <a href="government.html">Public sector</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Why: three facts -->
<section class="section photo-band" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <Photo name="monsoon" alt="" class="band-photo" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" />
  <a class="credit mono" href="https://www.pexels.com/photo/urban-flooding-in-a-residential-area-38551008/" rel="noopener">Dhaka. Photo: Faisal Ibne Kalam (Pexels)</a>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">The problem</span>
      <h2 id="why-title">Working devices, doing nothing</h2>
      <p>Every home has a drawer of them. Left there, they become waste. Left plugged in and never updated, they become a risk.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="fig" data-count="367" data-suffix="M kg">367M kg</div><p>of e‑waste in Bangladesh in 2022. Very little of it was formally recycled, and much of it still worked.</p><cite>Global E‑waste Monitor 2024</cite></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="fig" data-count="1" data-suffix="M+">1M+</div><p>home devices hijacked into a botnet that rents out people's internet to criminals.</p><cite>FBI, BADBOX 2.0 warning, June 2025</cite></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="fig">0</div><p>new devices we need to manufacture. The hardware already exists and is already paid for.</p><cite>Some jobs need one extra part, such as a storage disk.</cite></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- The garden-variety TV box: what's inside, and what it can do (scroll-driven) -->
<section class="bp bp-scroll tvbox" id="tvbox" aria-labelledby="tvbox-title">
  <div class="wrap bp-sticky">
    <div class="bp-text">
      <span class="kicker">01  Give it a job</span>
      <h2 id="tvbox-title">Take the TV box in your drawer.</h2>
      <p class="lede">It's a small computer. Here's what's inside, and what it can do again.</p>
      <ol class="bp-steps tv-steps">
        <li class="on"><h3>The box in the drawer</h3><p>Plenty of homes that moved to a smart TV still have one. Here's what's inside a typical box.</p></li>
        <li><h3>A small computer, really</h3><p>Four ARM cores, 1–4 GB of memory, flash storage, Ethernet, USB and Wi‑Fi. Roughly a phone from a few years ago, without the screen or battery.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Add a disk</h3><p>Its own flash is small and wears out. A USB disk gives it room for a whole family's photos and files.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Back up every phone</h3><p>Photos and files from the family's phones copy home every night.</p></li>
        <li><h3>A photo library</h3><p>Albums and a timeline on your own disk, with no monthly storage bill.</p></li>
        <li><h3>No ads, anywhere at home</h3><p>Every phone and TV on your Wi‑Fi, without installing anything on them.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Films and music at home</h3><p>Your own media library, played on any TV or phone in the house.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Rent out what's left</h3><p>Spare memory and disk earn credit by holding other members' encrypted backups.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
