<!-- Blueprint: devices drawn and wired in as you scroll -->
<section class="bp bp-scroll" id="how" aria-labelledby="bp-title">
  <div class="wrap bp-sticky">
    <div class="bp-text">
      <span class="kicker">01  Give it a job</span>
      <h2 id="bp-title">Every other device in the drawer, too.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Phones, routers, tablets and laptops go through the same steps: collected, wiped, rebuilt for one job, and connected to one network that we look after.</p>
      <ol class="bp-steps">
        <li class="on"><h3>Old phone → stairwell camera</h3><p>A phone from a few years ago still has a better camera than cheap CCTV. Wiped and mounted, it watches the stairs.</p></li>
        <li><h3>TV box → shop menu screen</h3><p>Plugged into an old TV, it shows today's prices or menu, updated from the owner's phone.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Wi‑Fi router → rooftop Wi‑Fi</h3><p>Rebuilt with open software that still gets security updates, it covers the roof and the guard room.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Tablet → lobby notice board</h3><p>Committee notices and the water schedule, on the wall where everyone sees them.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Laptop → building server</h3><p>Its battery rides out load-shedding while it records the cameras and keeps the backups.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
