<section class="section band" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq-layout">
    <div class="faq-side">
      <span class="kicker">FAQ</span><h2 id="faq-title">Questions people ask</h2>
      <figure class="faq-photo"><Photo name="teastall" alt="A roadside tea stall in Dhaka with a painted kettle on a blue wall." loading="lazy" maxWidth={1200} /><figcaption class="mono"><a href="https://www.pexels.com/photo/lonely-man-at-a-dhaka-tea-stall-33006139/" rel="noopener">Dhaka. Photo: Ahnaf Abror (Pexels)</a></figcaption></figure>
      <p class="small">Something else? <a href="contact.html">Ask us on WhatsApp</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>How does earning work?</summary><div><p>A device you choose rents out spare disk space, and from 2028 spare computing, to people who need it. It all happens inside a sandbox that can't see your files. You earn credit off your plan, and later cash by bKash.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>We're a company. What can you do with our old devices?</summary><div><p>Three things: put them back to work in your office, rent out their idle capacity overnight, or retire them with a wipe certificate per device, with the working ones going to school labs. <a href="companies.html">For companies</a></p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Will my device still work the way it used to?</summary><div><p>Usually not. It gets one new job, for example as a camera or a home server. If you still use a device every day, keep it and give us a spare.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Is this safe for my data?</summary><div><p>Your files stay on your own device at home. Copies stored in other members' homes are locked with a passphrase only you know, so the people storing them can't read them. And we erase every device's old data before it gets a new job.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens during load-shedding?</summary><div><p>Small devices can run from the same mini UPS that keeps your router on, and laptops have their own battery. Anything else shuts down safely and starts again when the power comes back.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What if I stop paying?</summary><div><p>You keep your devices and everything on them. We help you move anything you need, then remove our access.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens to devices you can't reuse?</summary><div><p>We keep useful parts for repairs and send the rest to a formal e‑waste recycler, with a receipt.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

